<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka forex market closed for Buddhist holiday.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka forex market closed for Buddhist holiday.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's foreign exchange market was shut on Thursday to mark a Buddhist holy day.</p>
<p>The rupee ended Wednesday at 57.33, after opening at 57.12, driven down by speculative demand for the dollar and slight import covering, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank has pushed up the dollar by 22 cents in the last 10 working days, in line with international movements dealers said.</p>
</text>
